codex
- servers/dev-home.sh:38 — Only the first fetch URL is checked; extra `remote.origin.url` entries and stale `remote.origin.pushurl` entries survive when it matches. Fix: inspect all configured values, normalize origin to exactly one intended fetch URL, and remove stale push URLs.

- servers/dev-home.sh:38 — `remote get-url` applies `url.*.insteadOf` rewrites. Writing the literal URL with `set-url` does not override those rules, so the effective origin can remain wrong and every invocation can repeat the mutation. Fix: inspect applicable configuration and ensure effective fetch and push URLs resolve to the intended repository; fail explicitly if an inherited rewrite cannot safely be corrected.

- servers/dev-home.sh:38 — A clone with no `origin` cannot be repaired: `get-url` fails inside the comparison, then `set-url` fails because the remote does not exist, terminating under `set -e`. Fix: detect a missing origin and use `remote add origin "$REPO_URL"`.

- servers/dev-home.sh:38 — Under `DRY_RUN=1`, `as_dev` prints a preview instead of executing `get-url`. Command substitution captures that preview, so the comparison always fails and reports a URL change even for a correct clone. Fix: perform existing-clone reads through a read-only helper that bypasses `run`; keep mutations behind `as_dev` and skip reads requiring a clone only previewed for creation.

VERDICT: FINDINGS
